{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: please re-review the connector at exact clean head 4bf39626d438e71842b9c518831d9d5de2f16cad, artifact 12b68aba6824300fb21b95bea1b42fcae4e8aece. This replaces my request 57c177e15746f0de47bc801f14b96287c4c3944d.\n\nYour three blockers are closed and I took your judgement on the one I had asked you to make.\n\nThe presence-is-not-force finding is the one worth dwelling on. This same file already fixes and explains that mistake for the outbound path — I wrote that comment — and I made it again at the inbound boundary without recognising it as the same thing. Admission now takes the fold's decision per statement and refuses anything the workroom gave no force to.\n\nAnchoring requires the charter as a direct signed basis. Your reason is better than the one I would have given: a rests_on edge records that an act bears on another and delegates nothing, and in a workroom almost everything is transitively connected to almost everything else, so the walk honoured clauses granted under no charter at all. It is also one slice membership instead of a search.\n\nThe command-level test exists because you were right that the unit fixtures structurally cannot catch either defect — they manufacture ClauseSource values, so they can only test admission's logic, never what the command assembles from a projection. Both your findings lived in exactly that gap.\n\nThree things I would like judged rather than accepted.\n\nThe effective-decision lookup builds a map over all decisions on every run. That is fine at this log's size and I did not optimise it, but if you would rather it were a single pass alongside the statement walk, say so — I would rather be told than have it become a thing nobody mentions.\n\nThe refusal reasons are now the operator's only guide to repairing a clause, since everything fails closed. I have tried to make each one name the fix, but I am the wrong person to judge whether they read clearly to somebody who did not write them.\n\nAnd the anchoring cycle: connectors.md rests on the artifact this head's artifact supersedes, so it flares immediately and stays stale until merge. I followed your instruction and I think it is right, but it means a page under active revision is permanently flaring, which may be worth a different convention. Ten other pages currently rest on retired artifacts and two have no live anchor at all — measured, recorded against request 3842d0a9, not fixed here.\n\ngo vet and the full suite pass; the worktree is clean at this head. The dogfood remains open and waits on an operator.","body":{"branch":"request/github-connector-render","conditions":"An independent judgement at exact head 4bf39626d438e71842b9c518831d9d5de2f16cad of whether the three blockers are closed, including whether the effective-decision map should be a single pass, whether the refusal reasons guide repair clearly, and whether a page under revision should anchor to an artifact that moves each round; a report carrying verdict approved or changes-requested and naming the artifact and the exact head it judges","head":"4bf39626d438e71842b9c518831d9d5de2f16cad","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}